# gap9-triggers: complete trigger vocabulary both engines

## What already existed (verified, not redone)
- cnc-core/src/trigger_records.rs carries the complete code space: 33-event
  `EventKind`, 37-action `ActionKind`, from_code/code/name/param_kind, parse and
  round-trip for every code.
- cnc-core/src/trigger_apply.rs `apply_action_record` dispatches all 35
  implemented ActionKinds through the `TriggerHost` trait; unknown codes call
  host.note() and report applied=false (never silent).
- Mapping-table tests from commit 609e2c2 pin every row of both tables:
  ra_eventtable_complete, ra_actiontable_complete, td_eventtable_complete,
  td_unmapped_documented.

## Engine implementation state (verified this pass)
- RA implements 23 of the 35 TriggerHost arms (win, lose, win_lose, all_hunt,
  create_team, destroy_team, reinforcements, drop_zone, fire_sale, destroy_trigger,
  text_trigger, reveal_map/area/zone, launch_nukes, special_weapon, note, ...).
- The remaining 12 families (allow_win, autocreate, begin_production,
  creep_shadow, destroy_object, play_movie, play_music, play_sound, play_speech,
  force_trigger, preferred_target, base_building) fall through to the trait's
  default arms, which call reject("<family>") - i.e. explicitly documented, never
  invented, matching the plan's "unmapped count drops to documented-only".
- TD likewise implements its arms (Action::Win/Lose/CreateTeam/AllToHunt/
  Airstrike/... game.rs:2494-2525) and its loader reports unmapped rows by
  original name (scenario_loader.rs:287,338).

## New acceptance test
- `ra_trigger_actions_execute` - a replayable script fires ten actions
  end-to-end through apply_action_record on a live Game (reveal all, all hunt,
  drop zone, fire sale, destroy trigger, create team, text trigger, reveal zone,
  launch nukes, fire special), then win closes the mission, then an unknown code
  is reported not-applied. Unknown-row and documented-rejection behavior pinned.

